{% comment %}
  Renders the UGC video row for the product page, reading its content from
  the main product section's fuel05_ugc and fuel05_ugc_video blocks. The
  hosting wrapper div (with the fuel05-ugc reveal classes) lives at the two
  render sites, not here.

  Accepts:
  - section: {Object} the main product section (required)
  - product: {Object} the page's product, read by the audience filter (required)
  - mode: {String} 'desktop' or 'mobile'; mobile adds the Visa alla link
  - with_assets: {Boolean} emit the stylesheet and script tags; pass it on exactly
    one of the two render sites per page, or the product page loads both twice.
    The desktop site owns it because it comes first in the markup. render gives a
    snippet its own scope and increment counters do not cross it, checked on the
    preview, so the guard has to be a parameter and cannot be a page level flag.

  Usage:
  {% render 'fuel05-ugc-pdp', section: section, product: product, mode: 'mobile' %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign heading = 'Älskad av tusentals'
  for b in section.blocks
    if b.type == 'fuel05_ugc' and b.settings.heading != blank
      assign heading = b.settings.heading
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The tiles are built first and the row is only printed if something came out of
  the loop. A clip that carries an audience tag is skipped on products without
  that tag, so a product matching none of them would otherwise get a heading and
  an empty slider under it. Building the markup once and testing it is also the
  only way the count and the output cannot drift apart; a separate scan loop
  would let the two rules disagree the next time one of them changes.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture tiles -%}
  {%- for b in section.blocks -%}
    {%- if b.type == 'fuel05_ugc_video' -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign wanted_tag = b.settings.audience_tag | strip | downcase
        assign show_tile = true
        if wanted_tag != blank
          assign show_tile = false
          for product_tag in product.tags
            assign have_tag = product_tag | downcase
            if have_tag == wanted_tag
              assign show_tile = true
              break
            endif
          endfor
        endif
      -%}
      {%- if show_tile -%}
        {% render 'fuel05-ugc-tile',
          video: b.settings.video,
          video_url: b.settings.video_url,
          poster: b.settings.video_poster,
          product_item: b.settings.product
        %}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign tiles = tiles | strip -%}

{%- if tiles != blank -%}
  {%- if with_assets -%}
    {{ 'fuel05-ugc.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
    <script src="{{ 'fuel05-ugc.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
  {%- endif -%}
  <div class="fuel05-ugc__inner">
    <div class="fuel05-ugc__header">
      <h2 class="fuel05-ugc__heading">{{ heading | escape }}</h2>
      <div class="fuel05-ugc__nav">
        <button class="fuel05-ugc__arrow fuel05-ugc__arrow--prev" type="button" aria-label="Föregående">
          <svg preserveAspectRatio="none" overflow="visible" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M9 4L17 12L9 20" stroke="black" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </button>
        <button class="fuel05-ugc__arrow fuel05-ugc__arrow--next" type="button" aria-label="Nästa">
          <svg preserveAspectRatio="none" overflow="visible" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M9 4L17 12L9 20" stroke="black" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="fuel05-ugc__slider swiper">
      <div class="swiper-wrapper">
        {{ tiles }}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  {%- if mode == 'mobile' -%}
    <a class="fuel05-ugc__visa-alla" href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/best-sellers">Visa alla</a>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
